    <section id="home">
        <h2>Welcome to BioRenew!</h2>
        <p>
            BioRenew is a student-led environmental initiative that focuses on turning 
            organic waste into renewable energy. Our goal is to promote sustainable 
            waste management practices while developing practical solutions that benefit 
            both the community and the environment.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="mission">
        <h2>Our Mission</h2>
        <p>
            To educate and empower communities in adopting innovative, eco-friendly 
            technologies that transform biodegradable waste into useful energy sources.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="about">
        <h2>About Us</h2>
        <p>
            BioRenew was founded by students from the Technological University of the Philippines 
            who are passionate about sustainability and environmental engineering. This project was 
            developed as part of our academic research focusing on renewable energy production using 
            organic waste.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Our Vision:</strong> A future where waste becomes a valuable source of clean energy.</p>
        <p><strong>Our Objectives:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Promote sustainable waste management.</li>
            <li>Develop low-cost renewable energy solutions.</li>
            <li>Spread environmental awareness through educational outreach.</li>
            <li>Encourage innovation in green technology.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="project">
        <h2>Our Project</h2>
        <p>
            Our research focuses on converting organic waste into renewable energy through 
            anaerobic digestion, producing biogas that can be used for cooking, electricity, 
            or heating. We aim to develop an affordable model that communities can adopt.
        </p>
        <h3>Features:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Efficient breakdown of organic waste.</li>
            <li>Biogas generation for energy use.</li>
            <li>Environment-friendly and low-cost system design.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Technologies Used:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Biogas digester system</li>
            <li>Gas storage and pressure valves</li>
            <li>Sensors for monitoring temperature and pH</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

